## SECTION 1 — SYSTEM GOAL

  - Purpose: build a Python clean-room CLI runtime that delivers practical, high-fidelity headless coding-agent
    behavior: multi-turn model+tool orchestration, explicit permissions, safe local execution, and resumable sessions.
  - “High-fidelity headless Claude-Code-like runtime” means:
      - deterministic event-driven session loop
      - robust local tools (Bash/Read/Edit/Write/LS/Grep/Glob)
      - strict deterministic permission decision engine (ask/auto/bypass)
      - append-only transcript + reliable resume/continue
      - retry/fallback/interrupt/timeout behavior that survives real failure modes
  - v1 user experience must deliver:
      - one-command headless workflow (ccr ...) for terminal users and scripts
      - stream-json mode for machine integration
      - permission decisions with auditable reasons
      - reliable recovery after interruption or transient provider failures
  - Intentionally excluded in v1:
      - TUI parity
      - updater/release ecosystem features
      - plugin marketplace UX
      - desktop integrations
      - full MCP transport/runtime (moved to v1.5)
      - full OS-level sandbox (moved to v2)

  ———

